<title>AUSTRIA: Kuwait says Equat petchen plant to be commissioned July 1997.</title>
<headline>Kuwait says Equat petchen plant to be commissioned July 1997.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kuwaiti Oil Minister Isa al-Mazeedi said on Thursday the Equate petrochemical plant, a joint venture with Union Carbide Corp, would be commissioned in July 1997.</p>
<p>A group of Western, Asian and Arab banks in September agreed to lend $1.2 billion for the complex, owned 45 percent by Union Carbide, 45 percent by Petrochemical Industries Co of Kuwait and 10 percent by private Bubiyan Petrochemical Co.</p>
<p>The plant will produce 650,000 tonnes a year of ethylene, 450,000 tonnes of polyethylene and 350,000 tonnes of ethylene glycol.</p>
<p>The total project cost is $2 billion.</p>
</text>
